{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791072006,"nonce":"prkCKQa8MbbSPeq01KVYuD0ibY4=","title":"BLADE cache reused across programs in one process breaks the thread stdlib","message":"compiler/examples/test_sys_thread compiles each case as its own program in one process. With CompilationConfig::default() (cache on) the first case passes and every later case crashes in haxe.EventLoop.__init__ (fault 0x10: main.thread reads null). Uncached, all 22 cases pass, and `rayzor run` with the cache on works across separate runs.\n\nThe thread stdlib is an import cycle (sys.thread.Thread \u003c-\u003e haxe.EventLoop \u003c-\u003e sys.thread.ThreadCallback), so its modules compile through failed attempts and retries. The second program in the process loads cached artifacts the first saved; what diverges was not pinned down. test_sys_thread now runs uncached.\n\nRepro: set test_sys_thread's config back to CompilationConfig::default(), `rm -rf .rayzor`, run the example.","files":null}]}